TopoSZp-CUDA — Example Programs
=================================

All example programs are built by CMake when both CUDA and OpenMP are available:

    mkdir build && cd build
    cmake .. -DENABLE_CUDA=ON
    make -j

The built executables are placed in the build directory.


Programs
--------

test_cuda_topology
    End-to-end 2D topology preservation test. Runs the full CUDA pipeline
    (find critical points, sort, compress, decompress, post-process) and
    verifies preservation rates against the OpenMP reference.

    Usage: test_cuda_topology <input_file> <rows> <cols> <errBound> <blockSize>
    Example: ./test_cuda_topology CLDHGH_1_1800_3600.dat 1800 3600 1e-3 64

test_cuda_topology_3d
    End-to-end 3D topology preservation test. Uses 6-connected neighborhoods
    and includes saddle stencil restoration with axis-pattern detection and
    3x3x3 RBF Gaussian kernel.

    Usage: test_cuda_topology_3d <input_file> <d1> <d2> <d3> <errBound> <blockSize>
    Example: ./test_cuda_topology_3d volume_100_500_500.dat 100 500 500 1e-3 64

test_cuda_compress
    Compression validation. Compresses with CUDA random-access mode,
    decompresses with both CUDA and OpenMP, and cross-validates results.
    Supports both absolute and relative error bounds.

    Usage: test_cuda_compress <input_file> <nbEle> <errBound> <blockSize>
    Example: ./test_cuda_compress data.dat 6480000 1e-3 64

test_cuda_decompress
    Decompression validation. Tests OpenMP-compress-to-CUDA-decompress and
    CUDA-compress-to-CUDA-decompress paths. Optionally tests topology-
    preserved decompression when grid dimensions are provided.

    Usage: test_cuda_decompress <input_file> <nbEle> <absErrBound> <blockSize> [rows cols]
    Example: ./test_cuda_decompress data.dat 6480000 1e-3 64 1800 3600

compare_with_lopc
    2D comparison tool. Benchmarks TopoSZp CUDA against the LOPC GPU
    compressor for critical point preservation, local order, compression
    ratio, and persistence analysis.

    Usage: compare_with_lopc <orig> <lopc_decomp> <rows> <cols> <eb> <blockSize> <lopc_comp_size>

compare_with_lopc_3d
    3D comparison tool. Same as above for 3D structured grids with
    6-connected neighborhoods.

    Usage: compare_with_lopc_3d <orig> <lopc_decomp> <d1> <d2> <d3> <eb> <blockSize> <lopc_comp_size>

compare_critical_points
    CPU-only utility. Compares critical points between original and
    decompressed data files without running compression (built even
    without CUDA).

    Usage: compare_critical_points <orig_file> <decomp_file> <rows> <cols> <eb>


Error Bound Modes
-----------------
Programs that accept <errBound> support two modes:
    Absolute:  1e-3          Maximum pointwise error is 0.001
    Relative:  rel:1e-4      Error bound = (data_max - data_min) * 1e-4


Input Data Format
-----------------
All programs expect raw binary files of 32-bit IEEE 754 floats in row-major
(C) order. For 3D data, the layout is d1 x d2 x d3 (slowest to fastest
varying dimension).
